// The soundtrack's instruments: every sound the band can make, by name.
// Songs (moods.ron) and the composer pick instruments by these names; a new
// entry here on an existing engine is a new instrument, no code needed.
// Edit and save: the running game picks it up within a second (the drum and
// note-block samples are rendered once, at startup).
//
// Each entry:
//   name    what songs call it.
//   bus     the mixer bus it plays through (a name from mix.ron's `buses`).
//   send    reverb send; echo: the dotted-eighth echo send.
//   pan     where it sits, -1 left .. 1 right:
//             at + (note - note.0) / note.1 + (random - 0.5) * rand,
//             then limited to +-clamp, then times scale.
//   voice   Poly: any free voice. Lead: the one mono lead voice of its engine
//           (Fm or Sub). Bass: one note at a time, never stolen (Fm).
//   glide   legato slide time in seconds for notes marked glide (None: re-strike).
//   bright  how far the band's brightness opens it: Fm Poly/Bass index
//           x (1 + bright * (b - 0.5)); Fm Lead x (1 - bright / 2 + bright * b);
//           Sub cutoff x 2^(bright * (b - 0.5)).
//   engine  the synthesis engine and its settings:
//     Fm(..)      2-operator FM with feedback, drawbars and tremolo (DX7 style).
//                 pitch_decay: higher notes die sooner (tines, bars).
//     Sub(..)     saws/square/sub through a swept state-variable filter.
//     String(..)  plucked string (Karplus-Strong, two polarisations, a body).
//     Blown(..)   a breathy pipe (flute, bottle, pan flute).
//     Choir(..)   three detuned singers through "oo"-to-"ah" formants
//                 (oo, ah: three (Hz, damping, level) each).
//     Kit(samples, hit)    synthesized drum samples: one per root note, from a
//                          generator `make` (Kick, Snare(wires, tone), Hat, OpenHat,
//                          Crash, Ride, Clap, Shaker, Membrane(hz, decay, drop,
//                          slap), Rim, Cowbell, Swell, Timbale(hz), Cajon(slap),
//                          Tabla(bayan), Tambourine, Guiro, Claves, Woodblock(hz)),
//                          scaled to `peak`.
//     Foley(recipe, hit)   foley-synth note-block samples rendered at `notes`.
//     hit: pitched (plays at the note, else always its root), push (how hard
//          it ducks the band, the sidechain), tone_floor (Hz a soft hit is
//          low-passed to), chokes (cuts choked voices), choked (an open hat).
